    "# TrustFact — Week 3: LIAR Data Audit and Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
    "**CPSC 59000 · Fall 2026 · Sabin Adhikari & Mohammad Hasan Ali Alshaggah**\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements the Week 3 tasks in the full proposal: **acquire and validate LIAR, inspect missingness and duplicates, study labels and statement lengths, examine topics and speakers, and save tables/figures**.\n",
    "\n",
    "The original TSV splits remain unchanged. This notebook **does not train or evaluate models**, and no results should be claimed until cells have been executed on your files. Run cells from top to bottom (Kernel → Restart & Run All)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ede36fd5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Imports and project paths\n",
    "Installed first in your selected environment: `python -m pip install pandas numpy matplotlib seaborn ipykernel`.\n",
    "\n",
    "Project must contain `data/raw/liar/train.tsv`, `valid.tsv`, and `test.tsv`. The notebook works whether VS Code starts it in the project root or the `notebooks` folder."
   ]
  },
